: " fully"}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.295180Z", "seq": 68, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": " replaced"}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.295180Z", "seq": 69, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": " ["}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.300633Z", "seq": 70, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": "2"}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.300633Z", "seq": 71, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": "]["}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.305635Z", "seq": 72, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": "3"}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.305635Z", "seq": 73, "node": "generate", "type": "token", "payload": {"text": "]."}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.354974Z", "seq": 74, "node": "generate", "type": "node_end", "payload": {"model": "gpt-4.1-mini", "cost_usd": 0.000408, "tokens_in": 744, "latency_ms": 2407.622099999571, "tokens_out": 69, "tokens_cached": 0}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}, {"ts": "2026-11-14T16:40:47.355985Z", "seq": 75, "node": null, "type": "done", "payload": {"answer": "A reducer in LangGraph state controls how node updates merge into the state. Each key in the state has its own reducer. Without a reducer, updates simply overwrite the previous value. Reducers define the logic for merging updates rather than replacing them outright, enabling partial updates to be combined into the existing state rather than fully replaced [2][3].", "citations": [{"n": 2, "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#reducers", "title": "Graph API overview", "section": "State > Reducers", "chunk_id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api#chunk-8"}, {"n": 3, "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#default-reducer", "title": "Graph API overview", "section": "State > Reducers > Default reducer", "chunk_id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api#chunk-10"}], "total_cost_usd": 0.00040818, "total_latency_ms": 8010.926200004178, "counterfactual_cost_usd": null}, "request_id": "d7d8d414-65c7-4de8-b131-705557ab7ab0"}], "chunks": [{"id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api#chunk-10", "doc_id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api", "title": "Graph API overview", "section": "State > Reducers > Default reducer", "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#default-reducer", "text": "The default reducer replaces the left value with the right. Nodes return partial updates, not the full state.\n\nFor example, start with `{\"foo\": 1, \"bar\": [\"hi\"]}`. An update of `{\"foo\": 2}` yields `{\"foo\": 2, \"bar\": [\"hi\"]}`. A later `{\"bar\": [\"bye\"]}` yields `{\"foo\": 2, \"bar\": [\"bye\"]}`."}, {"id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api#chunk-8", "doc_id": "doc-langgraph-graph-api", "title": "Graph API overview", "section": "State > Reducers", "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#reducers", "text": "Reducers control how node updates merge into state. Each key has its own reducer. With no reducer, updates overwrite the previous value."}]}